From: OpenWrt XG-040G-MD
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: air_en8811h: reconfigure LED gpio direction after MCU restart

The EN8811H LED pins are configured as outputs exactly once, in .probe():

	/* Configure led gpio pins as output */
	ret = air_buckpbus_reg_modify(phydev, EN8811H_GPIO_OUTPUT,
				      EN8811H_GPIO_OUTPUT_345,
				      EN8811H_GPIO_OUTPUT_345);

.config_init() restarts the MD32 MCU on every call but the first, and the
restart resets those pin directions back to input:

	/* If restart happened in .probe(), no need to restart now */
	if (priv->mcu_needs_restart) {
		ret = en8811h_restart_mcu(phydev);
		...
	} else {
		priv->mcu_needs_restart = true;
	}

Nothing ever configures them again. The LEDs therefore work only until the
PHY is re-attached for the first time and stay dark from then on. On the
Nokia XG-040G-MD the 2.5G port is attached three times during a normal
boot, so the LED is already gone by the time userspace is up:

	[    9.854911] lan1: PHY [mt7530-0:0f] driver [Airoha EN8811H] (irq=POLL)
	[   15.469915] lan1: PHY [mt7530-0:0f] driver [Airoha EN8811H] (irq=POLL)
	[   21.468161] lan1: PHY [mt7530-0:0f] driver [Airoha EN8811H] (irq=POLL)

Forcing the LED on through sysfs does not help: air_led_brightness_set()
writes the rules to the PHY registers just fine, but the pins are inputs so
nothing lights up. Unbinding and rebinding the driver does bring the LED
back, since that runs .probe() again -- which is what pointed at the pin
directions in the first place.

Move the pin direction setup into .config_init(), past the MCU restart.

--- a2/drivers/net/phy/air_en8811h.c
+++ b2/drivers/net/phy/air_en8811h.c
@@ -957,13 +957,6 @@
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
-	/* Configure led gpio pins as output */
-	ret = air_buckpbus_reg_modify(phydev, EN8811H_GPIO_OUTPUT,
-				      EN8811H_GPIO_OUTPUT_345,
-				      EN8811H_GPIO_OUTPUT_345);
-	if (ret < 0)
-		return ret;
-
 	return 0;
 }
 
@@ -1039,6 +1032,17 @@
 		return ret;
 
 	ret = en8811h_config_serdes_polarity(phydev);
+	if (ret < 0)
+		return ret;
+
+	/* Configure led gpio pins as output. en8811h_restart_mcu() above
+	 * resets the pin directions, so this cannot be done once in .probe()
+	 * as it used to be: every .config_init() after the first one left the
+	 * pins as inputs and the LEDs stayed dark for good.
+	 */
+	ret = air_buckpbus_reg_modify(phydev, EN8811H_GPIO_OUTPUT,
+				      EN8811H_GPIO_OUTPUT_345,
+				      EN8811H_GPIO_OUTPUT_345);
 	if (ret < 0)
 		return ret;
 
